# Copy this file to `.env`, fill in real values there, and NEVER commit `.env`.
# This file (.env.example) carries key NAMES only — no values — and is safe to commit.
#
# Where each secret lives (ruled 2026-10-18):
#   - Locally: `.env` in this repo, for `apify run` / `apify push` and manual wiki pulls.
#   - Unattended: GitHub Actions repository secrets, each scoped to one workflow:
#       maintainer daily check (deterministic): APIFY_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
#       maintainer repair (manual trigger):     the above plus CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
#       weekly wiki pull:                       none — the Store endpoints it reads are public
#     Nowhere else. Never on the Grok Bot computer (shared files and credentials across bots).
#   - The repo hook in .claude/settings.json denies Read and Bash access to `.env*` files by
#     NAME. It is a heuristic and misses indirect reads (dotenv loaders, `source`); it is not
#     the only guard. Side effect: any Bash command whose text mentions `.env` is denied, so
#     edit this file with the Write tool, not a shell heredoc.

# --- Apify ---
APIFY_TOKEN=                 # apify push, maintainer fixture runs, setting an actor's kill switch and description

# --- Telegram (escalations, repair requests, candidate pings, weekly summary) ---
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- Claude Code on the runner (repair workflow only) ---
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=     # from `claude setup-token` on the existing subscription: no new spend.
                             # An ANTHROPIC_API_KEY route is new recurring spend and needs a ruling.
